# A run directory is output, never input. `mqt-scpd plan -o artifacts/<chip>`
# writes everything below, and re-running the stages reproduces all of it, so
# none of it belongs in the repository. The 69-qubit capacity plan alone is
# seven megabytes.
#
# This file lives here rather than in the root `.gitignore`, which an external
# template owns.

# Stage artifacts
*.fb

# Renderings of a stage or of the plain layout
*.svg
*.gds
*.gds2
*.oas

# What `plan` copies in beside them: the chip input and the configuration the
# run was made from
00-chip.json
config.toml

# What `plan -d` draws: one picture per search, an HTML viewer per picture and
# the three dashboards that index them. The 45-qubit chip alone comes to five
# gigabytes of it, and `-d` reproduces all of it from the same artifacts.
debug/
*.html

# The measurement arms of 2026-10-04 (`logs/<arm>/<chip>.log`, one directory an
# arm) and the dev overlay under `dev/` — a copy of the installed package and
# run directories of their own — are output: every arm reproduces from the
# installed build and the benchmark configs. The scripts that run and read the
# arms are kept: `run-arm.sh`, `dev-sync.sh`, `dev-run.sh`, `dev-mqt-scpd.py`,
# `keylines.sh`, `arm-table.py`, `repair-summary.py`, `calibration.py`,
# `fcross.py`, `pinch.py`, `around.py`, `bends.py`.
logs/*
!logs/*.sh
!logs/*.py
dev/
